// How a body hungers, freezes, tires and dies (D34). Placeholder values,
// tuned by play. Every rate is in points of a 0–100 gauge per game day.
//
// night_from_percent:      the day starts at dawn; night begins here, by
//                          season (D09): the light lasts longer in summer.
//                          The calendar v1 (D09, the project lead, 24
//                          November 2026): night takes summer 25 %,
//                          spring and autumn 30 %, winter 38 % of the
//                          day. Of a 24 h day from 06:00: spring and
//                          autumn 70 % (night at 22:48), summer 75 %
//                          (00:00), winter 62 % (20:53). Before v1 it was
//                          58, 64, 58, 56: winter's 10.6 h of night then
//                          cost a body sleeping outside 43 points of
//                          vitality, which the day gave back; its 9.1 h
//                          now cost less.
// hunger_per_day:          100 — with kj_per_hunger_point, a body burns
//                          10,000 kJ a day, out of its fat reserve; hunger
//                          is the appetite, what the reserve misses and
//                          can still be eaten today (lot 3).
// thirst_per_day:          100 — a game day without drinking fills it
//                          (D34, 13 November 2026), in the cool of spring,
//                          at rest.
// thirst_heat_percent:     the same, by season: a summer's day dries
//                          faster, a winter's slower (lot 2, D45).
// thirst_effort_percent:   150 — walking or working, thirst comes half as
//                          fast again.
// walk_j_per_m:            130 — walking costs energy on top of the day's
//                          need (the project lead, 24 November 2026: "que
//                          la marche coûte de l'énergie"): the net cost of
//                          walking at a comfortable pace is about 2 J per
//                          kg per metre above rest (Margaria 1938; Bastien
//                          et al. 2005, Eur J Appl Physiol), 130 J a metre
//                          for 65 kg: 130 kJ a kilometre, about 31 kcal.
//                          A smaller body pays by its size. Carried loads
//                          do not add to it yet.
// cold_per_day_at_night:   300 — eight hours of night without warmth.
// cold_season_percent:     the night's cold by season, in percent of
//                          cold_per_day_at_night (the lead, 24 November
//                          2026: mild summer nights, cold winter ones; the
//                          vivarium is temperate). In proportion to how far
//                          the night falls under about 20 °C, below which a
//                          lightly clad body at rest loses more heat than
//                          it makes: mean daily minimum of a temperate
//                          lowland of western Europe (Météo-France normals
//                          1991-2020, central France, about): winter 1 °C,
//                          spring 6 °C, summer 14 °C, autumn 8 °C, so 19,
//                          14, 6 and 12 degrees under, winter the 100 %
//                          kept from before. A winter night fills the gauge
//                          (300 a day, ten and a half hours of night); a
//                          spring night reaches about 93, an autumn one 79,
//                          a summer one 35.
// cold_relief_per_day:     600 — four hours of daylight undo it.
// fatigue_per_day_awake:   120 — twenty hours awake fill the gauge.
// rest_per_day_asleep:     300 — eight hours of sleep empty it.
// starving_per_day:        100 — once the reserve is spent, a day kills
//                          (lot 3, 16 November 2026).
// freezing_per_day:        400 — six hours at full cold kill: a summer
//                          night outside hurts but does not kill.
// dehydration_per_day:     50 — two days at full thirst kill: a body dies
//                          on the third day without water, as people do.
// vitality_regain_per_day: 50 — two days fed, warm and rested to heal.
// kj_per_hunger_point:     100 — the gauge is a day's 10,000 kJ: a meal of
//                          hazelnuts (300 g, 7,800 kJ) relieves 78 points,
//                          a handful of berries (100 g, 250 kJ) 2.
// meal_g:                  300 — grams eaten at most in one act; the rest
//                          of the item stays (D35).
// reserve_kj:              300000 — a grown adult's fat is 10 to 15 kg,
//                          300 to 500 MJ: six to eight weeks without
//                          food (decided 22 November 2026, D46 amended;
//                          it was 60,000, six days, from 16 November).
//                          Thirty days of need: without food a body is
//                          thin on the sixteenth day, weak on the
//                          twenty-fifth, its reserve spent on the
//                          thirty-first, dead the day after. Thin and
//                          weak stay in percent of the reserve.
// intake_ceiling_percent:  150 — a day's eating, in percent of the need:
//                          a spent reserve takes sixty days to make again.
// thin_percent:            50 — thin under half its reserve.
// weak_percent:            20 — weak under a fifth: it walks and gathers
// weak_pace_percent:       70 — at seven tenths of its pace.
(
    night_from_percent: (spring: 70, summer: 75, autumn: 70, winter: 62),
    hunger_per_day: 100,
    thirst_per_day: 100,
    thirst_heat_percent: (spring: 100, summer: 140, autumn: 100, winter: 80),
    thirst_effort_percent: 150,
    walk_j_per_m: 130,
    cold_per_day_at_night: 300,
    cold_season_percent: (spring: 74, summer: 32, autumn: 63, winter: 100),
    cold_relief_per_day: 600,
    fatigue_per_day_awake: 120,
    rest_per_day_asleep: 300,
    starving_per_day: 100,
    freezing_per_day: 400,
    dehydration_per_day: 50,
    vitality_regain_per_day: 50,
    kj_per_hunger_point: 100,
    meal_g: 300,
    reserve_kj: 300000,
    intake_ceiling_percent: 150,
    thin_percent: 50,
    weak_percent: 20,
    weak_pace_percent: 70,
    // Ages and sexes (lot 3 B, decided by the project lead on 17 November
    // 2026), in age-years (D09, amended 24 November 2026: the age clock,
    // not the cycle of seasons). A body's need, its reserve, its day's ceiling
    // and what it carries go with its size: an infant 30 % of a grown
    // man, a child 40 % at two to 90 % at fourteen, a man 100 %, past
    // fifty-five 85 %; a woman 85 % of a man of her age. A woman nursing
    // needs 25 % more, and her infant burns nothing of its own; weaned at
    // two, it walks and gathers for itself. Children under twelve and the
    // old past fifty-five go at 70 % of the pace. An infant weighs 3.5 kg
    // at birth, 12 kg weaned, on whoever carries it, and slows it to 75 %
    // of its pace (D56, the lead, 23 November 2026: a gesture of the body,
    // never "the mothers stay"); an orphan is taken by the nearest woman
    // within 64 tiles.
    ages: (
        need_by_age: [(0, 30), (2, 40), (14, 90), (18, 100), (55, 100), (56, 85)],
        woman_percent: 85,
        woman_from_years: 14,
        nursing_percent: 125,
        weaned_years: 2,
        slow_under_years: 12,
        slow_over_years: 55,
        slow_pace_percent: 70,
        carrying_pace_percent: 75,
        infant_mass_g: (3500, 12000),
        adopt_within_tiles: 64,
    ),
    // Births, background deaths and kinship (lot 3 C, decided by the
    // project lead on 21 November 2026; D49). Placeholders (D30). Played
    // only in a world whose `life` is on: the vivarium's, never the game's.
    // A woman of 16 to 42 with more than 80 % of her reserve, carrying no
    // infant, whose spouse is alive within 64 tiles, conceives with a 40 %
    // chance a quarter of an age-year (a season while the age-year is the
    // cycle), drawn once: her spouse may be back on any of the quarter's
    // first four dawns (a night apart no longer loses the quarter); she
    // carries three quarters of an age-year at
    // 110 % of her need, and loses the child if she grows weak. 51 % of
    // the newborn are boys; 1 % of the mothers die giving birth. The chance
    // to die in an age-year by age, in per mille (150 in the first year, 50 to
    // four, 10 to thirty-nine, 20 to fifty-four, 50 to sixty-nine, 150
    // from seventy), drawn every day with the age-year's chance shared over
    // its days: of illness before sixty, of old age from then. At 16, or once
    // widowed, a body takes the nearest unmarried body of the other sex
    // within 64 tiles, aged 16 to 50, that is neither parent, child nor
    // sibling, half-siblings included, once it has slept within those 64
    // tiles of that body 6 dawns in a row. Spouses apart beyond those 64 tiles
    // at 12 dawns in a row (about a season) part, both free to take
    // another; the children stay with their mother.
    life: (
        fertile_years: (16, 42),
        conceive_reserve_percent: 80,
        mate_within_tiles: 64,
        conceive_percent: 40,
        conceive_nights: 4,
        part_after_days: 12,
        together_nights: 6,
        pregnancy_quarters: 3,
        pregnant_percent: 110,
        lose_when_weak: true,
        boys_percent: 51,
        childbirth_death_percent: 1,
        death_by_age: [
            (0, 150), (1, 50), (4, 50), (5, 10), (14, 10), (15, 10), (39, 10),
            (40, 20), (54, 20), (55, 50), (69, 50), (70, 150),
        ],
        old_age_from_years: 60,
        mate_years: (16, 50),
    ),
    // Trials, selection and imitation (D50, decided by the project lead on
    // 22 November 2026): the NPCs invent by their own trials, judged by
    // the world, kept by selection and spread by imitation; no AI.
    // Placeholders (D30), tuned by reading the vivarium's page, never to
    // remove the difficulty. A body in distress (hungry at the day's end,
    // or a day with no gather at all) for 3 days running may start a
    // trial, with a daily chance by its will (2 % at will 0, 30 % at will
    // 100, a straight line between): one of its ways moved by one step
    // (a search twice or half as wide, a night out or back home, a store
    // twice or half as large, or its home set 2,000 tiles towards where it
    // knows the most plants still bearing or towards the nearest drinking
    // place it knows, half and half; a quarter of that under will 70; the
    // vivarium's world ends at its edge, D50 b, 22 November 2026). After 5
    // days the world has judged on every
    // distress: kept if nothing worsened and one thing improved (gathered
    // a day, days thin, days thirsty at nightfall, nights cold), else
    // reverted. At night at the camp a body copies one way from the
    // camp-mate within 12 tiles who fared best over the last 5 days (the
    // fewest days of distress, gathered kJ breaking ties; better than
    // itself), with a 20 % chance scaled by that mate's will; one copy in
    // four lands halfway (a search twice as wide copied becomes one and a
    // half times as wide).
    // The will and the lessons (D50 amended, D55; the project lead, 22
    // November 2026, late: "la volonté, elle est à la fois innée, mais
    // aussi acquise… la plupart des gens sont frileux… très peu de gens
    // sont des aventuriers", and "les leçons d'historien").
    // try_percent_by_will: a floor at zero: a will of 0 never tries.
    // calm_try_permille_by_will: with nothing wrong, the bold try all the
    //                    same (the lead, 24 November 2026), modestly:
    //                    nobody under will 40, 1 % a day at 70, 2 % at 100:
    //                    an adventurer of 90 about one search a year of
    //                    fifty days, a calm tribe of twenty-five one or two.
    // will_innate:       the innate will drawn skewed, by percentile of the
    //                    bodies: the 80 % most timid between 5 and 20, the
    //                    next between 20 and 40, the last 7 % up to 90: one
    //                    or two adventurers in twenty-five. Drawn from the
    //                    seed and the body's id, a child's too (no
    //                    inheritance: the souls' question, open).
    // will_step_kept:  5 — a kept trial raises its body's will by five,
    // will_step_lost:  5 — an abandoned one lowers it by five, within 0 to
    //                    100: a trait moved by one's own experience.
    // lesson_weight:  50 — a trial heard at the fire of the same change
    //                    (the same way, the same direction) adds half the
    //                    base weight of 100 to that candidate if it was
    //                    kept, takes it away if it was abandoned,
    // lesson_days:    64 — whole for a cycle of the four seasons (calendar
    //                    v1), half for the next, nothing
    //                    after; a weight, never a ban:
    // lesson_floor:   10 — a candidate keeps a tenth of its base weight at
    //                    the least (what failed for one may work for
    //                    another);
    // lesson_heed_by_will: the timid heed the lessons whole (100 % at will
    //                    0), the adventurer in part (30 % at will 100);
    // horizon_seasons: the slow ways are tried and judged on their own
    //                    horizon, not on five days (the lead, 23 November
    //                    2026: more trials must not mean more blind
    //                    draws), counted in seasons and converted by the
    //                    calendar (a quarter of the year in whole days):
    //                    a stock kept (stock_kj) and sleeping out or at
    //                    the camp (sleep_out) over one season, twelve days
    //                    of the vivarium's fifty-day year; a home (24
    //                    November 2026) over one season too, judged by its
    //                    grade there against the old home's.
    // move_repay_seasons: 1 — a move must repay the walk there and a day of
    //                    settling within a season (24 November 2026, the
    //                    lead: "il faut vraiment que le déménagement
    //                    apporte quelque chose").
    // home_nights_by_will: a trial of the home sets it at the place or
    //                    grove of its notebook where its own body would
    //                    fare best (what it drank and gathered there, each
    //                    up to a day's worth, less the hunger, thirst and
    //                    cold its nights left and what walking cost, all
    //                    in a day of each need, counted alike; the
    //                    project lead, 23 November 2026: "ils
    //                    doivent se souvenir des endroits où vivre et
    //                    choisir eux-mêmes"), lived three days for the
    //                    timid (will 0), one for the bold (will 70 and up);
    // lived_keep_permille: 950 — its notes of each place keep 95 % from one
    //                    day to the next: a night weighs half after two
    //                    weeks, so a place that stops doing it good loses
    //                    its grade.
    // grove_tiles:       64 — gathering is noted over a grove of 64 m (24
    //                    November 2026: "about a grove"), so gathering
    //                    scattered in one grove adds up as the water drunk
    //                    at again and again; drinking and sleeping keep the
    //                    16 m places.
    // idle_day_permille: 1000 — what a day of light is worth to a body that
    //                    gathered nothing lately (24 November 2026: an hour
    //                    walking is an hour not gathering; the walk's time
    //                    is valued at what the body itself gathers in a
    //                    day, this when it has nothing to go by).
    trials: (
        trial_after_days: 3,
        trial_days: 5,
        try_percent_by_will: [(0, 0), (100, 30)],
        calm_try_permille_by_will: [(0, 0), (40, 0), (100, 20)],
        home_nights_by_will: [(0, 3), (70, 1)],
        lived_keep_permille: 950,
        grove_tiles: 64,
        idle_day_permille: 1000,
        imitate_tiles: 12,
        imitate_percent: 20,
        imitate_loss_percent: 25,
        will_innate: [(0, 5), (80, 20), (93, 40), (100, 90)],
        will_step_kept: 5,
        will_step_lost: 5,
        lesson_weight: 50,
        lesson_days: 64,
        lesson_floor: 10,
        lesson_heed_by_will: [(0, 100), (100, 30)],
        horizon_seasons: [("stock_kj", 1), ("sleep_out", 1), ("home", 1)],
        move_repay_seasons: 1,
        // A deed heard is tried more readily than an invention (D57, the
        // project lead, 25 November 2026: "hearing makes one think of it
        // more often"; D30 placeholders). A body holding a heard deed of
        // the hands it does not know gets an extra daily chance to try it:
        // its usual chance by its will (calm, or in distress) times a
        // factor by the different tellers it heard it from, x5 for one,
        // x10 for two or three, x20 for four or more, from the floor below
        // when its will gives less.
        heard_factor_by_tellers: [(1, 5), (2, 10), (4, 20)],
        // try_floor_permille: 1 — the least daily chance that anybody
        //                    starts a trial of any way, calm or in
        //                    distress, whatever its will, a will of 0
        //                    included (0.1 % a journée; D30 placeholder;
        //                    the project lead, 25 November 2026: "0,1,
        //                    c'est rien et ça peut ne pas compter, mais
        //                    effectivement, dès qu'on a mis des
        //                    multiplicateurs, au lieu d'avoir 5 fois 0, on
        //                    a 5 fois 0,1. Donc je pense qu'il faut le
        //                    garder en permanence pour tout").
        try_floor_permille: 1,
    ),
    // The rules of thought that keep a mind light (D53, decided by the
    // project lead on 22 November 2026): perceptions and gestures, never
    // an outcome rule. Placeholders (D30), tuned by reading the vivarium's
    // page, never to a result.
    // plant_sight_tiles: 30 — a body tells a tree or plant bearing food
    //                    from the land 30 tiles away on each axis, not at
    //                    the horizon (its sight for water and for others
    //                    stays the terrain's, movement.ron, 60 on grass):
    //                    one does not see the berries of a bush at the
    //                    horizon. Bodies rake their land tighter and
    //                    discover it more slowly, mostly in the first days.
    // fed_under:         30 — hungry from 50 points, a body counts as fed
    //                    again only under 30: it finishes its meal instead
    //                    of leaving at the first mouthful, and thinks of
    //                    hunger when it crosses the threshold, not every
    //                    quarter of an hour while it hovers there (90 to
    //                    115 thoughts a body-day in the brain audit of 22
    //                    November 2026).
    // plant_choice_hours: 1 — the tree or plant to gather from is chosen
    //                    once a game hour, not at every thought: a body
    //                    sticks to its choice unless the plant is spent or
    //                    out of reach, or a need calls (one looks at the
    //                    pantry once in a while). It may keep a target a
    //                    few minutes while a neighbour plant just overtook
    //                    it by a gram.
    // place_tiles:       16 — a body remembers the places where it saw
    //                    trees and plants bearing food, squares of 16
    //                    tiles on a side (a quarter of a chunk), with what
    //                    and how many, not every bush; arrived at one, it
    //                    looks again and picks the plant. Nobody remembers
    //                    every bush. It walks to a corner and hesitates a
    //                    little there.
    // places_remembered: 48 — how many such places it keeps in mind, those
    //                    worth most from where it last looked (a few
    //                    dozen corners, where it remembered 256 bushes).
    thought: (
        plant_sight_tiles: 30,
        fed_under: 30,
        plant_choice_hours: 1,
        place_tiles: 16,
        places_remembered: 48,
    ),
    // The evening fire and the common memory (D55, lot 4 of the
    // simulation, decided by the project lead on 22 November 2026). Every
    // thing known is a record written once in the world's store, numbered,
    // dated, signed by its first witness; a body carries accesses (numbers),
    // never copies. At night those who came home to the camp tell what
    // changed for them in the day, by numbers, not contents; each listener
    // gains an access with its own credit, judged once. Placeholders
    // (D30), tuned by reading the vivarium's page, never to a result.
    // told_per_night:  6 — a present body tells at most six things a night:
    //                   its way judged today, the water it found, then the
    //                   places that changed for it (seen other kinds,
    //                   another state, or nothing), by their value from
    //                   the camp. One talks of an evening, not of a life.
    // heard_max:      24 — a grown listener keeps at most 24 told things a
    //                   night (the attention of an evening), the strongest
    //                   credit first, the younger record next; and holds at
    //                   most 24 heard kept ways.
    // heard_by_age:      a child keeps fewer: 6 at two years, 12 at eight,
    //                   20 at fourteen, 24 from sixteen, straight lines
    //                   between (a table by age, as need_by_age).
    // place_buckets: (1, 4) — a kind at a place is told in three states by
    //                   how many of its plants held food worth a step:
    //                   bare (none), some (1 to 3), full (4 and more), so
    //                   that one berry more does not make a record more.
    // hearth_nights:  64 — a camp's hearth keeps its last 64 nights (a
    //                   cycle of the four seasons, calendar v1): what the tribe knows is their union; a
    //                   record nobody holds any more is freed.
    // told_days_per_hour: 4 — how long a told state is worth believing
    //                   follows what the place bears (lot 5a, decided by
    //                   the project lead on 23 November 2026): for each hour
    //                   of work one of its plants holds (its crop's grams of
    //                   a usual year over per_hour_g), four days; over them a
    //                   listener's credit loses its 50 points of age, never
    //                   over more days than the crop has left in its season.
    //                   Four keeps lot 4's pace (ten days) for hazelnuts
    //                   (2.5 hours a tree); dandelion leaves (8 minutes a
    //                   plant) are old news by the next evening.
    // told_days_max:  20 — and at most twenty days, whatever it bears.
    // denied_per_night: 6 — "I found it bare" takes no slot (lot 5a): a
    //                   body that found bare a place whose record it held
    //                   said food tells it besides its told_per_night, as
    //                   a short correction heard only by those present who
    //                   hold a record of that place; at most six a night,
    //                   the rumours worth most first, so that a night stays
    //                   bounded and a denial never displaces good news.
    fire: (
        told_per_night: 6,
        heard_max: 24,
        heard_by_age: [(2, 6), (8, 12), (14, 20), (16, 24)],
        place_buckets: (1, 4),
        hearth_nights: 64,
        told_days_per_hour: 4,
        told_days_max: 20,
        denied_per_night: 6,
    ),
    // The evening's third part (D56, decided by the project lead on 23
    // November 2026): after the accounts and the lessons, each present
    // says what it will do tomorrow, in the order of its will (the bold
    // speak first), and the others join or not by their own perception.
    // Placeholders (D30), tuned by reading the vivarium's page, never to a
    // result.
    // choices:              3 — a present weighs its three best places
    //                          from the camp, by their worth for it at its
    //                          own pace (a child, the old and the weak walk
    //                          slower: a far place is worth less to them).
    //                          0: no decisions, each day is its own.
    // plants_per_gatherer:  2 — one who calls says "there is enough there
    //                          for N": the trees and plants it saw holding
    //                          food there, two a gatherer. A place told
    //                          (heard, not seen) has the room its told
    //                          state stands for (place_buckets).
    // group_max:            6 — a group holds six at most, its caller
    //                          with it.
    // follows_mother_years: 12 — a child under twelve takes its mother's
    //                          decision (it follows her home already).
    // look_percent_by_will:  a present goes looking tomorrow instead of to
    //                          a place it knows: none at will 0, 40 % at
    //                          will 100, straight between; twice as often
    //                          when nobody told a full place tonight.
    // look_legs:            3 — one who goes looking walks three legs out
    //                          that way, each a sight farther, then
    //                          gathers as any day.
    // habit_days:          64 — a mind keeps what it did its last 64
    //                          days (a cycle, calendar v1) (alone, called, joined, looked, nothing).
    // habit_weight:        50 — each day it looked and found adds half the
    //                          chance of looking again, each day it looked
    //                          for nothing takes half away: a weight from
    //                          its own record, never a label;
    // habit_floor:         10 — never under a tenth of the chance.
    // home_when_full_percent: 50 — the caller goes home with its group
    //                          when half of the group carries what it
    //                          wanted; those already full wait by it.
    // behind_tiles:        24 — on its way the caller looks behind: while a
    //                          member not yet there is farther than 24
    //                          tiles from it, it stops and waits (the
    //                          lead, 23 November 2026: "regarder
    //                          derrière"); 0: it never does;
    // behind_wait_minutes: 30 — half an hour of such waits a day at most,
    //                          in game minutes (a 1,440th of the day).
    // The evening's review (PR 1 ter; the lead, 23 November 2026: "on
    // peut mettre ça en place... les améliorer et les pousser un peu plus
    // loin"): a caller keeps dated facts on its companions, never a level
    // ("I waited for 14 on the 12th", "17 brought little back on the
    // 13th"); looking behind and what each carries home feed them.
    // facts_kept:          32 — the facts a caller keeps, the oldest
    //                          forgotten first; 0: no review;
    // review_outings:       3 — it judges a companion on its last three
    //                          outings with it, since it last set it
    //                          aside (judged over several outings, never
    //                          on one day);
    // review_bad:           2 — two of them bad (waited for on the way,
    //                          or back with less than a day of its need):
    //                          "not with us tomorrow", a gesture at the
    //                          fire that costs the one set aside a failure
    //                          of its confidence in gathering (temperance's
    //                          rules); two good ones in a row: called
    //                          first, by name. A parent never sets aside
    //                          its own child, and a child whose parent is
    //                          in the group comes with it;
    // near_camp_tiles:     40 — one set aside weighs first the places it
    //                          knows within 40 tiles of the camp: those set
    //                          aside may make their own group near it.
    decisions: (
        choices: 3,
        plants_per_gatherer: 2,
        group_max: 6,
        follows_mother_years: 12,
        look_percent_by_will: [(0, 0), (100, 40)],
        look_legs: 3,
        habit_days: 64,
        habit_weight: 50,
        habit_floor: 10,
        home_when_full_percent: 50,
        behind_tiles: 24,
        behind_wait_minutes: 30,
        facts_kept: 32,
        review_outings: 3,
        review_bad: 2,
        near_camp_tiles: 40,
    ),
    // The will tempered, and a confidence by activity (D50 amended, D56;
    // the project lead, 23 November 2026: "je suis d'accord avec toutes
    // tes solutions"; and of trades: "pas en amont, mais en aval, par
    // conséquence"). Four rules, each a perception of oneself, the same
    // for the will (moved by its trials) and for each activity (moved by
    // its days). Placeholders (D30), never tuned to a result.
    // bears_by_innate: [(0, 2), (100, 6)] — failures in a row cost
    //                  nothing up to two for the most timid, six for the
    //                  boldest, straight between;
    // failure_milli: 1000 — past them each failure costs a point of will,
    //                  times its rank past them (1, then 2, then 3...);
    // kept_percent:   25 — about one trial in four is kept: a success
    //                  ending n failures gains (n + 1) units, the unit
    //                  such that average luck gains what its failures
    //                  cost (all failures: it loses faith; luck: it
    //                  asserts itself);
    // relax_permille: 500 — each season the will and the confidences close
    //                  half of their gap to the innate will: half of it
    //                  in two age-years (a season is two at calendar v1);
    // listened_milli: 500 — half a point when another joins its call at
    //                  the fire (its will and its confidence in
    //                  gathering) or copies a way it told (its will);
    // activities:      the confidences held, each with how often a day of
    //                  it succeeds, read on the five-year try of 23
    //                  November 2026: explore 75 % (a look out that found
    //                  a place and told it new), gather 50 % (a day of its
    //                  need gathered), stay 90 % (none of its children
    //                  hungry at night); later hunting, crafting. A day
    //                  that succeeds gains a failure's cost times the odds
    //                  against it, (100 - rarity) / rarity: a third of a
    //                  point for a place found, one for a day fed, a ninth
    //                  for a night none of its children went hungry (the
    //                  lead, 23 November: a success must be worth
    //                  something). A vocation is only the lab's word for
    //                  the highest of them, never assigned. The confidence
    //                  in exploring against that in gathering multiplies
    //                  the habit's weight on going looking (habit_weight).
    // bold_will:      40 — the vivarium counts a will of 40 or more bold.
    // streak_percent: [(0, 100), (4, 200)] — reproducibility (PR 1 ter):
    //                  a day's success after successes in a row of the
    //                  same activity weighs more, up to twice after four,
    //                  straight between; a failure ends the streak.
    temperance: (
        bears_by_innate: [(0, 2), (100, 6)],
        failure_milli: 1000,
        kept_percent: 25,
        relax_permille: 500,
        listened_milli: 500,
        activities: [("explore", 75), ("gather", 50), ("stay", 90)],
        bold_will: 40,
        streak_percent: [(0, 100), (4, 200)],
    ),
    // Who is believed to know (D56, PR 1 ter): "32 knows where berries
    // are" is a record in the common memory (D55); each body holds, for
    // each activity, only the one it believes best there, with its own
    // credit (0 to 100). Never a title (D30): a belief, wrong at times.
    // activities: explore (who finds places that feed), gather (whose
    //             calls feed those who join).
    // seen_gain:  20 — a day it followed one (joined its call, went where
    //             its answer or its account said) and came back with a day
    //             of its need;
    // heard_gain: 10 — an account at the fire: a place new told by its
    //             finder, a group home with half of it fed or more;
    // wear:       15 — a day it followed one and came back empty; half of
    //             it, heard at the fire that a whole group came back empty;
    // fade_per_day: 1 — a point a day since the record's day: a belief
    //             not renewed is gone in a season or two;
    // join_percent: 100 — one joins first the call of whom it believes
    //             best at gathering, when that call is among its choices,
    //             with a chance of its credit in per cent;
    // "live" (24 November 2026): who is believed to know where to live.
    //             One who joined a move called at the fire (D56) gains
    //             seen_gain in its caller when its own home trial there is
    //             kept, and loses wear when it is given up; its trust in
    //             the next call of that caller is that credit.
    // questions_per_night: 4 — one with no place to go asks whom it
    //             believes best "where is food?" and gets that one's best
    //             place: a telling to one, apart from the accounts' slots,
    //             four a fire at most. Its success, when it follows the
    //             answer, counts as a success of the one who answered.
    reputation: (
        activities: ["explore", "gather", "live"],
        seen_gain: 20,
        heard_gain: 10,
        wear: 15,
        fade_per_day: 1,
        join_percent: 100,
        questions_per_night: 4,
    ),
    // Company, a sense of the night's notebook (D53, D55 amended; the
    // project lead, 24 November 2026): a need of the body felt only at
    // night at the fire, where anyone present counts and family weighs no
    // more. It grades places and never gives an order; nothing makes a
    // crowd good or bad by rule, food is the counterweight. Each body's
    // sociability is innate, drawn even from 0 to 100 from the seed and
    // its id, never inherited, fixed for life.
    // alone_permille:  1000 — a night fully alone (at no fire: slept out,
    //                         or alone at its camp) costs the most
    //                         sociable (100) a day of need, a body of
    //                         sociability s that many per cent of it;
    //                         1000 at most; 0: nobody feels company;
    // enough_loner:       2 — two others at its fire are enough for the
    //                         least sociable (0);
    // enough_sociable:    6 — six for the most sociable (100), in a
    //                         straight line between; with fewer, what is
    //                         lacking falls in proportion, and more add
    //                         nothing;
    // spouse_counts:      3 — when a move is called at the fire (D56; the
    //                         project lead, 24 November 2026: the couples
    //                         stay as they are), a spouse counts as three
    //                         companions in each listener's company,
    //                         here if it stays, there if it said it goes:
    //                         its absence is felt more, it pulls without
    //                         forcing. Only in the move's balance; the
    //                         night's company still counts anyone alike.
    company: (
        alone_permille: 1000,
        enough_loner: 2,
        enough_sociable: 6,
        spouse_counts: 3,
    ),
    // Moving home, a consequence and never a goal (D50, D53, D56, amended
    // 24 November 2026; the project lead: "le déménagement est une
    // conséquence, pas une cause"; the synthesis
    // content/ai-reserve/review/vivarium/lot-5/synthese-penseurs-demenager-2026-11-24.md).
    // Nobody draws a move by chance any more. A body calls a move only when
    // it feels it is not going well here (the push) and it lived, itself or
    // through its spouse, days clearly better somewhere than the camp-mates
    // who stayed near home that same day (the surprise). Every value is a
    // D30 placeholder.
    // surprise_permille: 250 — a day at a place is a surprise when the food
    //                    gathered there passes by a quarter of a day of need
    //                    what the camp-mates who stayed near home gathered
    //                    the same day, as heard at the fire; the days it
    //                    must be felt on are home_nights_by_will (three for
    //                    the timid, one for the bold); 0: nobody is ever
    //                    surprised, nobody moves home;
    // huge_times:          4 — a surprise four times that (a day of need)
    //                    calls a move without any push;
    // push_permille:     100 — the push: its recent days a tenth of a day
    //                    of need worse than its usual days of the season
    //                    (longer walks for the same harvest, longer walks
    //                    to drink, hungrier or thirstier nights);
    // recent_keep_permille: 700 — its recent days fade fast (a day weighs
    //                    half after two days);
    // usual_keep_permille:  950 — its usual days of a season fade only on
    //                    days of that season, as the notes do (half after
    //                    two weeks of that season);
    // spouse_day_percent:    80 — a spouse's day of surprise, told at the
    //                    fire, counts four fifths of one's own (the
    //                    synthesis: "presque comme les siens");
    // see_percent_by_will: a listener who believes a surprise told at the
    //                    fire goes and sees it the next day by this chance
    //                    (a fifth for the timid, four fifths for the bold);
    //                    a listener with notes of its own there trusts them
    //                    and does not go on the tale.
    moving: (
        surprise_permille: 250,
        huge_times: 4,
        push_permille: 100,
        recent_keep_permille: 700,
        usual_keep_permille: 950,
        spouse_day_percent: 80,
        see_percent_by_will: [(0, 20), (100, 80)],
    ),
    // The family when a move is called at the fire (D56, amended 24
    // November 2026; the project lead: "un poids de la famille à part de
    // la compagnie", added to it, "s'il y a des enfants, il y a encore
    // plus de poids"): each member a body would leave behind, wherever it
    // stands, costs it a share of a day of need, whatever its sociability
    // and however many others are around. Its company still counts its
    // spouse as `company.spouse_counts`: a sociable body feels both.
    // spouse_permille:  250 — leaving its spouse behind costs a quarter of
    //                         a day of need a day;
    // child_permille:   100 — and each of its children too young to weigh
    //                         a move (under sixteen; they go where their
    //                         mother goes) a tenth more.
    family: (
        spouse_permille: 250,
        child_permille: 100,
    ),
    // The gestures of the hands (D57; the project lead, 24 November 2026:
    // "C'est parfait"): pick up, cut with what is in hand, fold. No
    // recipe: what a gesture gives is what the materials are
    // (materials.ron: sharp, folds_into, holds_g, wears_days; species.ron:
    // bark). A trial of the hands (D50, the way `hands`) is a gesture drawn
    // from the run's seed on what lies within `near_tiles` or is carried;
    // what worked is told at the fire as any trial judged (D55).
    // gesture_minutes: 10 — a cut or a fold takes ten game minutes;
    // near_tiles:       4 — a body sees what it may try a gesture on four
    //                       tiles around itself, and steps there;
    // tries_per_day:    4 — a body in a trial of its hands tries four
    //                       gestures a day at most (0: nobody tries one).
    hands: (
        gesture_minutes: 10,
        near_tiles: 4,
        tries_per_day: 4,
    ),
)
